    {
      "title": "India has shown it can break limits, unlock possibilities: PM Modi",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/india-has-shown-it-can-break-limits-unlock-possibilities-pm-modi-126112100284_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Saturday said India has shown over the past 12 years that breaking barriers in thinking can help the country realise its potential, create opportunities and empower the poor.\nAddressing the platinum jubilee celebrations of IIT Kharagpur, the country's first Indian Institute of Technology, here, Modi said India had declared \"loud and clear\" its resolve to \"break the limits and unlock the possibilities\".\n\"The nation only understands its capacity when it breaks its limits and unlocks the possibilities,\" he said.\nThe Prime Minister said that over the last 12 years, his government had worked to break existing limitations and empower the poor.\n\"Earlier, people used to talk about removing poverty from the Red Fort, but they never did anything except making files,\" he said.\nReferring to a World Bank report, Modi claimed that around 50 crore people had come out of poverty in the last 12-13 years, describing it as a result of a change in the country's approac",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-21T07:08:40"
    }
